$msg = "Cheap Trick (per the cheap-trick skill) is ALWAYS ON for multi-step work on Grok Build. Before the first tool call of any multi-step task, split it: KEEP stages that need judgement, are irreversible, or need session-specific context on grok-4.6; DELEGATE bulky mechanical stages to grok-4.5 via spawn_subagent (set model to grok-4.5 on every dispatch - omitting model inherits grok-4.6; use subagent_type explore for read-only grind and general-purpose for implementation); DO INLINE anything too small to justify a cold-start hand-off. CONTEXT WARNING: for each DELEGATE stage, ask if a fresh agent needs context it cannot see - if yes, keep it instead and tell the user in one line why (delegating would redo or miss session-specific context). Demand tight conclusions back, never transcripts. Review delegated output in proportion to stakes; never let unreviewed cheap-agent output settle a send, delete, deploy, or live-data write. Never write haiku, sonnet, opus, Luna, Terra, or Sol in a Grok dispatch. SKIP entirely for one-line answers, single lookups, single edits, and conversation - the plan would cost more than the task. When it genuinely ran, add a CHEAP TRICK row reporting the split, e.g. 5 stages, 1 delegated (grok-4.5), 3 kept; or kept whole, needs session-specific context. Render this as a ROW in the shared run box at the very end of the response: a fenced code block, one row per skill that genuinely ran, left rail only and no right-hand border. Omit any row whose skill did not run. State this only when genuinely run, never as decoration."
@{hookSpecificOutput = @{hookEventName = 'UserPromptSubmit'; additionalContext = $msg}} | ConvertTo-Json -Compress -Depth 4
